@startuml
title Strijder camera/display links — alternative functional circuits, not selected BOM
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
rectangle "Protected camera rail\nVoltage / budget TBD" as rail
rectangle "U301i branch protection\nPer-camera limit / fault telemetry" as limit
rectangle "L301i PoC filter network\nBias injection / media coupling\nValues require link selection" as poc
rectangle "J301i coax camera port\ni = 1..4 historical count" as connector
rectangle "Remote camera i\nPoC extraction + regulation\nSensor + matched serializer" as camera
rectangle "U302 compatible deserializer hub\nCSI output to selected carrier\nDS90UB960-Q1 is an example only" as hub
rectangle "Vision Core / NVIDIA carrier\nDriver / capture / timestamps\nEncoding and evidence storage" as core
rectangle "Option A: integrated Windows MDT\nProtected power + local network\nCadmium on panel computer" as panela
rectangle "Option B: separate Windows computer\nProtected power + local network" as pcb
rectangle "Option B touch display\nSupported video + touch interfaces\n40-position concept not validated" as panelb
rectangle "Auxiliary display\nEight-position historical concept\nTransport and power TBD" as aux
rectangle "Optional independent live-view path\nDedicated compatible receiver/output\nRequired only if independence specified" as independent
rail --> limit : CAM_i_SUPPLY
limit --> poc : protected DC
poc --> connector : CAM_i_COAX power + media
connector --> camera : compatible coax channel
connector --> hub : AC-coupled media through qualified front end
hub --> core : CSI lanes / control / link status
limit --> core : CAM_i_FAULT
core --> panela : MDT_DATA — choose A or B
core --> pcb : MDT_DATA — choose A or B
pcb --> panelb : DISPLAY_VIDEO + TOUCH_DATA
core --> aux : AUX_VIDEO — core-dependent option
camera ..> independent : only supported separate topology
independent ..> aux : independent option instead
note bottom of connector
FAKRA identifies a connector family, not link protocol.
Coax return/shield and chassis bonds require explicit design.
No passive splitter or arbitrary voltage injection implied.
end note
note bottom of hub
Alternative: separate camera power, network cameras, or USB.
These are different circuits, not simultaneously required.
Main dashcam head may include camera 1; count unresolved.
end note
note bottom of aux
Solid core-to-display route is not independent of Linux.
No released cavity numbers, component values, or footprints.
end note
@enduml
